@ 8.5.2 - Proto-Turkic to Sakha
# citation: Pogostick Man, from Firespeaker.org wiki contributors (2014), “Turkic sound changes”.
	{e,ɤ}:[+long] > je (the second one is conjectured based on my admittedly sparse knowledge of P:[-voice]urkish; I can only guess that 〈ė〉 is some sort of back unrounded vowel)
	{ o, oɡ, ø, øɡ, iɡ } > { wo, ɥø, o:[+long], ø:[+long], i:[+long] }
	{ a{ɡ̌(ɯ),b}, {o{ɡ̌,b},aɡ̌u}, u{ɡ̌,b} } > { ɰa, wo, u:[+long] }
	iɡ̌ > ɯ:[+long]
	ɯ:[+long] > i:[+long] (but original ɯ:[+long] unaffected?)
	eɡ > je, i:[+long], ji
	d > t / V_V
	s > ∅ / V_V
	{ʃ,z} > s / V_V
	s > ∅ / #_
	{z,ʃ} > h
	j > s (possibly only initially?)